The following method is a correct implementation of the selection sort algorithm. The method correctly sorts the
elements of  arr  so that they appear in order from least to greatest.

public static void selectionSort(int[] arr) 
{ 
   for (int j = 0; j < arr.length - 1; j++) 
   { 
      int minIndex = j; 
      for (int k = j + 1; k < arr.length; k++) 
      { 
         if (arr[k] < arr[minIndex]) 
         { 
            minIndex = k; 
         } 
      } 
      int temp = arr[j]; 
      arr[j] = arr[minIndex]; 
      arr[minIndex] = temp; 
